  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_015 (pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.639 acc. We know transformer aggregation hurt performance with concat fusion (config_014: 0.579 vs config_033: 0.619), but that comparison confounds aggregation and fusion simultaneously. We have not tested transformer aggregation paired with weighted fusion. Question: config_048 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all else at the current best (pca_n2000, resnet50, weighted), cleanly isolating whether the aggregation–fusion interaction matters. Why best next: It is a single-variable extension of the top configuration (exploitation), directly answers whether avgpool is truly superior to transformer under weighted fusion, and the result will either confirm avgpool as the correct aggregation (guiding all future multimodal experiments) or reveal a hidden interaction that could unlock further gains. Under a tight budget, this clean A/B comparison against the current best is more informative than exploring an untested RNA encoder (scvi_n200) or a second image encoder, where the expected signal is smaller given the large gap already seen between pca_n2000 and scgpt."
